WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.635
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:08.905 --> 00:11.199
CREATIVE ONIGIRI SHOP BEEMUS

3
00:12.325 --> 00:13.451
Good morning.

4
00:13.535 --> 00:15.703
One Minami Minamida set, please.

5
00:16.204 --> 00:19.374
Where were you, Minami? Dressed like that?

6
00:19.457 --> 00:22.001
Our morning meeting was canceled,

7
00:22.085 --> 00:24.045
so there's no point going in early.

8
00:24.128 --> 00:25.880
So I went for a run.

9
00:25.964 --> 00:26.923
Right.

10
00:27.006 --> 00:30.176
So you haven't abandoned work again.

11
00:30.260 --> 00:32.011
I haven't quit quitting quitting!

12
00:32.554 --> 00:34.722
To prepare for my next case,

13
00:34.806 --> 00:36.558
I've been building stamina!

14
00:36.641 --> 00:38.434
You're certainly motivated.

15
00:39.227 --> 00:42.105
Your managing partner

16
00:42.188 --> 00:44.274
praised you on the phone the other day.

17
00:44.983 --> 00:45.817
Managing Partner?

18
00:45.900 --> 00:47.777
Persistent and creative, she said.

19
00:50.697 --> 00:53.324
Why were you on the phone with the managing partner?

20
00:55.118 --> 00:57.162
Hirokawa &amp; Howard LPC

21
00:57.245 --> 00:59.539
has 712 lawyers.

22
01:00.248 --> 01:03.168
Why would she speak to a rookie's father?

23
01:04.169 --> 01:05.295
Well…

24
01:05.378 --> 01:06.671
You see…

25
01:07.714 --> 01:10.133
I couldn't reach you on your phone,

26
01:10.216 --> 01:11.676
so I called the firm.

27
01:11.759 --> 01:12.844
She happened to answer.

28
01:13.928 --> 01:15.346
-Happened to? -Yes.

29
01:15.430 --> 01:17.015
-Answer? -Yes.

30
01:17.098 --> 01:18.224
Managing Partner?

31
01:20.226 --> 01:24.480
Maybe her secretary was out at lunch.

32
01:24.564 --> 01:26.900
It was around lunchtime.

33
01:28.776 --> 01:30.320
That's right.

34
01:30.945 --> 01:33.448
Your phone! Answer it. Go on.

35
01:40.830 --> 01:41.706
Hello?

36
01:41.789 --> 01:44.459
Morning, Ms. Minamida. Where are you?

37
01:45.001 --> 01:45.960
At home.

38
01:46.044 --> 01:47.962
What about the briefing?

39
01:48.046 --> 01:50.840
Today's meeting was moved to tomorrow.

40
01:50.924 --> 01:52.842
Mr. Himi told me.

41
01:52.926 --> 01:55.803
Yes, the meeting was canceled

42
01:55.887 --> 01:57.931
-because today… -Morning.

43
01:58.556 --> 02:01.226
Because a client visit came up at short notice today.

44
02:01.309 --> 02:03.436
We need a briefing beforehand.

45
02:04.896 --> 02:06.272
A briefing?

46
02:08.524 --> 02:09.359
Come in.

47
02:09.442 --> 02:10.526
Excuse me!

48
02:16.741 --> 02:18.117
Good morning!

49
02:18.201 --> 02:19.202
That outfit?

50
02:19.285 --> 02:20.328
I came in a rush.

51
02:20.411 --> 02:21.496
You ran here?

52
02:21.579 --> 02:24.207
Yes! I thought I had time this morning,

53
02:24.290 --> 02:25.667
so I went running.

54
02:25.750 --> 02:28.044
I'm not sure I follow,

55
02:28.127 --> 02:30.129
but leave yourself more time.

56
02:31.089 --> 02:32.507
I'm sorry.

57
02:34.717 --> 02:36.052
Mr. Himi.

58
02:36.135 --> 02:39.097
Why didn't you tell me about the briefing?

59
02:39.180 --> 02:40.473
I thought I did.

60
02:40.556 --> 02:42.183
You only mentioned the meeting.

61
02:42.267 --> 02:44.227
Maybe you weren't listening.

62
02:44.310 --> 02:46.271
All right. We're short on time.

63
02:46.771 --> 02:48.439
But Mr. Himi…

64
02:48.523 --> 02:51.275
Fine, let's leave it at that. Mr. Miyaji.

65
02:51.359 --> 02:52.860
Her documents, please.

66
02:52.944 --> 02:54.320
I'll give her a copy.

67
02:54.404 --> 02:55.697
Here you are.

68
02:59.867 --> 03:01.744
-I'll read them quickly. -No need.

69
03:01.828 --> 03:03.121
I'll explain briefly.

70
03:03.204 --> 03:05.581
Yes. Briefly, please.

71
03:08.376 --> 03:12.005
Our client is a major school, Ray Arrows Dance Academy.

72
03:16.134 --> 03:19.220
The other party runs a dance school too.

73
03:19.303 --> 03:21.139
Saty, a dancer and choreographer.

74
03:22.181 --> 03:25.601
She used to be Ray Arrows' star instructor.

75
03:25.685 --> 03:26.853
She went independent

76
03:26.936 --> 03:28.354
and in August,

77
03:28.438 --> 03:31.149
opened Fordee Dance Studio.

78
03:31.816 --> 03:34.485
She choreographs for pop idols,

79
03:34.569 --> 03:36.738
so she has some influence.

80
03:36.821 --> 03:39.866
She posted criticism of Ray Arrows online.

81
03:39.949 --> 03:40.867
SATY

82
03:40.950 --> 03:45.663
"Great times. 'Pro' teachers thrive just teaching the motions. ()"

83
03:45.747 --> 03:48.499
"It'd be interesting to require all instructors to be licensed."

84
03:48.583 --> 03:53.046
Those empty parentheses are slang. There's no "laugh" inside.

85
03:53.129 --> 03:55.298
It's sarcastic, "Not funny."

86
03:55.381 --> 03:58.426
They see it as defamation and business interference

87
03:58.509 --> 04:02.055
and want to sue Saty for damages.

88
04:02.138 --> 04:05.016
The client will be here shortly.

89
04:05.099 --> 04:07.643
Details then. I already told Mr. Himi,

90
04:07.727 --> 04:11.606
but you'll both be handling this case, Ms. Minamida.

91
04:11.689 --> 04:12.607
And you?

92
04:12.690 --> 04:14.776
I'm busy with another matter.

93
04:14.859 --> 04:16.694
Medical Association head Watagami, right?

94
04:16.778 --> 04:18.738
In that case, you can leave this one just to me.

95
04:18.821 --> 04:20.531
What? I'm doing it too!

96
04:20.615 --> 04:22.033
Then I'll leave it to you both.

97
04:22.116 --> 04:23.242
-Yes! -Yes!

98
04:34.003 --> 04:36.464
That Saty woman exaggerates

99
04:36.547 --> 04:38.591
to make herself look good.

100
04:39.092 --> 04:40.343
Even winning that contest,

101
04:40.426 --> 04:43.137
she takes all the credit for it,

102
04:43.221 --> 04:46.557
but she just did exactly what I advised.

103
04:46.641 --> 04:49.685
Really? So you were behind it, Chairman!

104
04:50.561 --> 04:53.272
Are you a professional dancer, then?

105
04:54.315 --> 04:55.149
What?

106
04:55.233 --> 04:57.944
Or, as Saty put it in her post,

107
04:58.027 --> 04:59.320
are you a self-proclaimed pro?

108
05:01.280 --> 05:02.240
Who is she?

109
05:03.658 --> 05:06.369
All our instructors are teaching professionals.

110
05:07.453 --> 05:10.039
Then "self-proclaimed" is insulting.

111
05:10.540 --> 05:13.334
To teach her a lesson in life,

112
05:13.418 --> 05:15.962
I say we make her pay a fortune.

113
05:16.045 --> 05:18.881
Agreed. Let's make her pay a fortune.

114
05:19.966 --> 05:24.137
But establishing defamation from this would be difficult.

115
05:24.762 --> 05:25.930
Even if we do,

116
05:26.013 --> 05:28.391
damages are usually a few hundred thousand yen.

117
05:28.474 --> 05:29.976
Hardly a fortune.

118
05:30.059 --> 05:34.397
Those posts damaged our school's brand.

119
05:34.480 --> 05:35.773
That's a fact.

120
05:35.857 --> 05:38.025
You want me to just take it?

121
05:38.109 --> 05:40.194
No, that's not what I mean…

122
05:41.279 --> 05:42.196
Chairman.

123
05:42.280 --> 05:44.657
To establish defamation

124
05:44.740 --> 05:46.742
and increase the damages,

125
05:46.826 --> 05:50.496
I searched Saty's old posts for anything

126
05:50.580 --> 05:52.790
that could be criticism of Ray Arrows.

127
05:53.666 --> 05:56.294
You investigated all of this?

128
05:56.794 --> 05:58.087
Yes. On my own.

129
05:58.171 --> 06:01.007
I wanted to be as prepared as possible.

130
06:01.090 --> 06:03.634
Just what I'd expect from a top firm.

131
06:07.305 --> 06:08.181
Mr. Himi.

132
06:08.264 --> 06:09.265
Yes?

133
06:09.348 --> 06:10.600
Very reassuring.

134
06:10.683 --> 06:11.976
You're too kind.

135
06:14.770 --> 06:16.189
Here's one I found.

136
06:17.190 --> 06:20.818
"Classes are too big. Students at all different levels."

137
06:20.902 --> 06:22.653
"Will you ever group them properly?"

138
06:23.863 --> 06:26.073
"Work hard. Get treated the same."

139
06:26.157 --> 06:29.535
"The best people keep leaving." There's more.

140
06:32.830 --> 06:35.791
Let's prove these posts are baseless!

141
06:35.875 --> 06:37.877
Yes. I'm counting on you.

142
06:37.960 --> 06:42.381
Of course. First, I'd like to speak with your staff.

143
06:42.465 --> 06:46.010
I'm driving back to the school. Want to come?

144
06:46.093 --> 06:48.346
May I? Thank you.

145
06:48.429 --> 06:49.513
I'll come too!

146
06:49.597 --> 06:50.973
I can do the interviews alone.

147
06:51.057 --> 06:51.974
But…

148
06:52.058 --> 06:53.476
I'll be right behind you.

149
06:53.559 --> 06:55.061
-See you shortly. -Yes.

150
06:55.144 --> 06:56.062
Mr. Himi…

151
06:56.145 --> 06:57.146
Thank you.

152
07:06.864 --> 07:07.698
Mr. Himi.

153
07:07.782 --> 07:10.535
Not seeing the documents beforehand put me at a disadvantage.

154
07:10.618 --> 07:12.995
Please share what you learn.

155
07:14.789 --> 07:15.623
I'd rather not.

156
07:16.749 --> 07:17.833
Rather not?

157
07:17.917 --> 07:21.546
This case came through a major client's referral.

158
07:22.338 --> 07:24.340
I need to score some points.

159
07:25.800 --> 07:29.345
You don't need to do anything this time. Bye.

160
07:35.560 --> 07:36.686
What now?

161
07:39.730 --> 07:42.233
I won't be outdone.

162
07:54.036 --> 07:56.455
Are you sure it's okay to come here uninvited?

163
07:56.539 --> 07:57.748
It's not a problem.

164
07:58.249 --> 08:03.004
We need to see if the person we're suing really would slander others.

165
08:03.087 --> 08:06.007
Looking into her character should give us a lead.

166
08:11.345 --> 08:12.597
CONSTRUCTION WATCH FOR TRUCKS

167
08:12.680 --> 08:15.349
Fordee Dance Studio is behind this hospital.

168
08:15.433 --> 08:16.851
WATAGAMI HOSPITAL

169
08:22.231 --> 08:23.441
Are you okay?

170
08:26.944 --> 08:29.155
I'm fine. Just startled.

171
08:30.114 --> 08:31.198
Let's go!

172
08:32.325 --> 08:33.367
Let's go.

173
08:34.035 --> 08:37.455
FORDEE DANCE STUDIO

174
08:37.538 --> 08:39.665
Hey! Going to class?

175
08:39.749 --> 08:40.750
Yeah. Bye!

176
08:47.256 --> 08:50.301
Are all these cars picking up children

177
08:50.384 --> 08:52.094
from Fordee Dance Studio?

178
08:53.262 --> 08:54.764
It's really popular.

179
08:54.847 --> 08:56.265
Yuma! Yuma!

180
08:57.099 --> 08:59.060
-You forgot this. -Thanks.

181
09:01.604 --> 09:04.023
Excuse me. Are you dropping off your child?

182
09:04.815 --> 09:07.193
Oh, my car? I'll move it right away.

183
09:07.276 --> 09:08.235
No.

184
09:08.319 --> 09:11.322
We're thinking of dance lessons for our child.

185
09:15.868 --> 09:18.287
What's Ms. Saty like as a teacher?

186
09:18.954 --> 09:22.416
Does she exaggerate or take credit for others' work?

187
09:23.042 --> 09:25.002
I don't think so.

188
09:25.086 --> 09:26.170
She's a good teacher.

189
09:26.253 --> 09:28.214
And an amazing dancer.

190
09:28.297 --> 09:30.925
Want to watch a lesson?

191
09:31.008 --> 09:32.551
ENROLL NOW! COME WATCH A CLASS

192
09:53.114 --> 09:55.574
This is more than a hobby class.

193
09:56.701 --> 09:59.161
Go, go, go! Push harder!

194
10:05.626 --> 10:07.086
Finish strong!

195
10:08.546 --> 10:10.756
Yeah! That's good!

196
10:11.424 --> 10:12.717
Yuma, you fell behind.

197
10:12.800 --> 10:13.718
-So close. -Yes.

198
10:13.801 --> 10:15.553
The rest was great, though.

199
10:15.636 --> 10:17.388
You're all geniuses!

200
10:18.431 --> 10:20.057
Five-minute break!

201
10:20.141 --> 10:21.016
Yes!

202
10:28.190 --> 10:30.735
-Was that helpful? -Yes!

203
10:30.818 --> 10:33.446
You were all so perfectly in sync!

204
10:33.529 --> 10:35.781
We represent the school, after all.

205
10:38.534 --> 10:40.953
We're entering this contest next month.

206
10:41.036 --> 10:44.290
Ms. Saty's class won it last year, right?

207
10:45.458 --> 10:47.543
We're aiming to win too.

208
10:50.129 --> 10:52.089
With that dance just now?

209
10:54.091 --> 10:55.634
With moves like this.

210
10:56.302 --> 10:58.262
That's quite an original take.

211
10:58.721 --> 10:59.847
Like this, right?

212
11:02.725 --> 11:04.894
Yes! Exactly! That's it.

213
11:04.977 --> 11:06.145
You're very good.

214
11:06.228 --> 11:07.396
Want to try it with us?

215
11:08.564 --> 11:10.816
-Yes, please! -What?

216
11:21.452 --> 11:23.078
Again!

217
11:23.162 --> 11:26.248
Hey! No adding members without asking!

218
11:27.750 --> 11:29.084
Sorry.

219
11:29.168 --> 11:30.169
Sorry.

220
11:31.003 --> 11:32.671
Lessons for your child?

221
11:33.589 --> 11:34.590
Yes…

222
11:34.673 --> 11:36.759
They're all so good.

223
11:36.842 --> 11:38.177
Are they aiming to go pro?

224
11:38.260 --> 11:39.762
Some want to.

225
11:39.845 --> 11:43.098
But even if they don't go pro,

226
11:43.182 --> 11:45.518
lessons should give them lasting skills.

227
11:46.644 --> 11:47.728
Lasting skills?

228
11:48.604 --> 11:50.689
Some schools don't even teach the basics.

229
11:50.773 --> 11:53.067
They just have kids move to music.

230
11:53.150 --> 11:54.860
There are plenty of schools like that.

231
11:55.611 --> 11:59.448
I want children to learn real dance.

232
11:59.532 --> 12:01.075
That's why I opened this.

233
12:02.868 --> 12:04.662
She seems like a good teacher.

234
12:04.745 --> 12:06.664
Yes, a good teacher.

235
12:06.747 --> 12:08.749
No rush to join.

236
12:08.832 --> 12:10.084
Visit other schools

237
12:10.167 --> 12:12.002
and choose what suits your child.

238
12:14.505 --> 12:16.966
Let's visit Ray Arrows too.

239
12:17.049 --> 12:18.592
They're famous too.

240
12:20.344 --> 12:22.513
I don't mean to interfere,

241
12:23.138 --> 12:26.141
but being famous doesn't make a school good.

242
12:30.062 --> 12:32.815
Break's over. Let's pick up where we left off.

243
12:32.898 --> 12:34.525
-Yes! -Line up.

244
12:34.608 --> 12:37.987
Unbelievable. You should've told me before going undercover.

245
12:41.156 --> 12:42.074
Well?

246
12:42.575 --> 12:44.243
Did you learn anything?

247
12:45.661 --> 12:49.707
Saty was quite unlike our client's description.

248
12:49.790 --> 12:51.750
Students and parents love her.

249
12:51.834 --> 12:54.503
They all said she's a good teacher.

250
12:54.587 --> 12:58.632
They're customers. Of course she'd be nice to them.

251
13:01.385 --> 13:04.013
Tell me what your interviews revealed.

252
13:04.096 --> 13:07.057
No. You didn't bring me anything useful,

253
13:07.141 --> 13:08.517
so it's hardly a fair trade.

254
13:08.601 --> 13:11.020
I need you to share your findings.

255
13:11.103 --> 13:15.274
Or did no one confirm that the posts were false?

256
13:15.357 --> 13:16.483
Someone did.

257
13:18.986 --> 13:20.863
Then share it with me.

258
13:21.989 --> 13:24.992
Ray Arrows may be hiding the truth

259
13:25.075 --> 13:28.120
and using a lawsuit to silence Saty.

260
13:29.246 --> 13:30.956
You think this is a SLAPP suit?

261
13:31.582 --> 13:34.335
I'm saying it's a possibility.

262
13:34.418 --> 13:36.712
No, that's not possible.

263
13:36.795 --> 13:37.921
Why not?

264
13:38.464 --> 13:41.717
A SLAPP is when a wealthy party

265
13:41.800 --> 13:45.346
drags out a case against someone poorer

266
13:45.429 --> 13:48.932
to wear them down and silence criticism.

267
13:49.016 --> 13:51.852
But how big are these two schools?

268
13:52.561 --> 13:54.355
-About the same. -Right.

269
13:54.438 --> 13:58.984
If this drags on, wouldn't Ray Arrows face the same financial burden?

270
13:59.068 --> 13:59.902
Yes.

271
13:59.985 --> 14:01.403
Exactly.

272
14:01.487 --> 14:05.949
Even if they hate her, that wouldn't be cost-effective.

273
14:06.033 --> 14:07.743
That's true, but…

274
14:08.661 --> 14:12.081
Trust the client who wants to proceed.

275
14:12.998 --> 14:15.709
Isn't that our duty as lawyers?

276
14:18.337 --> 14:19.463
Understood.

277
14:20.047 --> 14:22.716
No objections to proceeding, then?

278
14:31.725 --> 14:33.060
Among elite dancers,

279
14:33.143 --> 14:36.146
rivals are valued for pushing each other to improve.

280
14:36.230 --> 14:37.231
FIRST ORAL ARGUMENT

281
14:37.815 --> 14:41.193
The defendant's posts merely offer such encouragement.

282
14:41.777 --> 14:44.363
They don't damage anyone's reputation.

283
14:44.446 --> 14:45.864
Objection! On that point…

284
14:45.948 --> 14:47.366
-Case law… -Objection!

285
14:47.449 --> 14:48.409
Plaintiff's counsel!

286
14:48.993 --> 14:50.953
One at a time, please.

287
14:53.998 --> 14:55.207
I'll speak.

288
14:59.795 --> 15:03.590
Defamation depends on how the audience perceives it.

289
15:03.674 --> 15:04.550
The post says,

290
15:04.633 --> 15:08.220
"Great times. 'Pro' teachers thrive just teaching the motions."

291
15:08.303 --> 15:10.681
The empty parentheses at the end

292
15:10.764 --> 15:13.142
are common slang with no "laugh" inside.

293
15:13.225 --> 15:15.894
a sarcastic way of saying "not funny."

294
15:15.978 --> 15:19.148
Most readers wouldn't interpret that as encouragement.

295
15:19.231 --> 15:20.774
I would also add

296
15:20.858 --> 15:23.444
she has over 100,000 followers.

297
15:23.527 --> 15:26.864
Before today's hearing, it had over four million views,

298
15:26.947 --> 15:29.241
11,000 likes, and reposts…

299
15:29.324 --> 15:30.659
3,421!

300
15:30.743 --> 15:32.619
3,421 reposts.

301
15:32.703 --> 15:36.498
Saty's influence in the dance world is considerable!

302
15:36.582 --> 15:37.416
It is!

303
15:37.499 --> 15:38.959
Plaintiff's counsel.

304
15:39.626 --> 15:42.046
Only one of you may speak.

305
15:45.132 --> 15:46.383
Sorry.

306
15:47.760 --> 15:49.636
In light of this,

307
15:49.720 --> 15:53.348
we believe this post constitutes defamation.

308
16:00.898 --> 16:02.566
So you're lawyers.

309
16:05.110 --> 16:08.072
I don't appreciate being investigated like that.

310
16:08.155 --> 16:10.491
Many of our students are young children.

311
16:10.574 --> 16:12.868
Please take that into account.

312
16:12.951 --> 16:14.453
I'm sorry.

313
16:14.536 --> 16:15.579
Sorry.

314
16:15.662 --> 16:16.538
Besides,

315
16:16.622 --> 16:19.083
what's the point of this lawsuit?

316
16:19.166 --> 16:22.628
Right before a major competition, you sue us?

317
16:22.711 --> 16:24.171
That's pure harassment.

318
16:24.254 --> 16:25.964
You're the one harassing us!

319
16:26.048 --> 16:29.093
Smearing us with your false posts.

320
16:29.176 --> 16:30.761
I only wrote the truth.

321
16:30.844 --> 16:32.471
What truth?

322
16:32.554 --> 16:35.724
-You've started rumors! -They're worse than us.

323
16:35.808 --> 16:37.851
Aren't you the one lying?

324
16:37.935 --> 16:39.061
That contest win,

325
16:39.144 --> 16:41.647
I hear you've been taking credit for it.

326
16:41.730 --> 16:43.440
Have you ever danced?

327
16:43.524 --> 16:46.568
I'd never say such a thing.

328
16:46.652 --> 16:49.071
-I heard you did. -He did say it, right?

329
16:49.154 --> 16:51.448
-You believed him? -What?

330
16:51.532 --> 16:54.159
Mr. Himi, you knew he was lying?

331
16:54.243 --> 16:57.037
You said our duty was to trust clients.

332
16:57.121 --> 17:01.041
I'll fight to the bitter end, however long it takes!

333
17:05.629 --> 17:07.339
Lying is wrong!

334
17:08.048 --> 17:11.218
Mr. Himi, any other lies? Please tell me.

335
17:11.301 --> 17:14.638
Well… Not about the lawsuit, I think.

336
17:25.858 --> 17:27.192
This one?

337
17:29.194 --> 17:30.654
This one?

338
17:33.157 --> 17:34.199
You two!

339
17:34.283 --> 17:36.785
Clear some plates if you're just playing.

340
17:37.536 --> 17:38.537
We're not playing.

341
17:38.620 --> 17:40.372
We're practicing spotting lies.

342
17:40.873 --> 17:43.500
Spotting lies? Playing Old Maid?

343
17:43.959 --> 17:45.377
Minami, the eyes.

344
17:45.460 --> 17:47.421
The eyes will usually give them away.

345
18:00.267 --> 18:01.643
I still can't tell.

346
18:02.477 --> 18:06.106
Autistic people struggle to read expressions through eye contact.

347
18:06.190 --> 18:08.400
Minami, try the nose instead.

348
18:08.483 --> 18:09.693
The nose?

349
18:09.776 --> 18:13.322
They say lying releases catecholamines,

350
18:13.405 --> 18:16.533
which swell the tissue in your nose and make it itch.

351
18:16.617 --> 18:18.160
-The joker! -Listening?

352
18:18.243 --> 18:21.205
I've never seen anyone's nose swell or itch from lying.

353
18:21.788 --> 18:23.457
Pinocchio's grows.

354
18:32.674 --> 18:35.052
I win! Minami, you're terrible!

355
18:36.136 --> 18:37.763
How can you tell, Ririi?

356
18:37.846 --> 18:39.348
You're easy to read.

357
18:39.431 --> 18:40.599
Say something.

358
18:40.682 --> 18:42.059
I'll guess if it's a lie.

359
18:44.228 --> 18:45.312
Then…

360
18:47.064 --> 18:49.650
I don't want to lose to Mr. Himi.

361
18:49.733 --> 18:50.943
Mr. Himi? Who's that?

362
18:51.026 --> 18:53.028
We're working on a case together.

363
18:53.737 --> 18:56.490
But he won't share information,

364
18:56.573 --> 18:58.492
and I doubt he's investigated properly.

365
18:59.826 --> 19:03.038
So I'll have to redo the interviews tomorrow.

366
19:03.121 --> 19:04.915
I wouldn't want to lose to him.

367
19:04.998 --> 19:06.500
True or false?

368
19:06.583 --> 19:08.043
It's probably…

369
19:08.126 --> 19:09.628
True! That's true!

370
19:09.711 --> 19:11.421
Hey! Don't answer for me!

371
19:11.505 --> 19:13.548
Ririi and I are practicing.

372
19:13.632 --> 19:15.050
Please go away, Dad.

373
19:15.926 --> 19:17.177
Come on.

374
19:18.387 --> 19:19.846
Let's switch.

375
19:19.930 --> 19:22.557
You guess whether what I say is true or false.

376
19:23.392 --> 19:24.393
Okay.

377
19:29.648 --> 19:31.275
Minato Funai…

378
19:32.859 --> 19:35.279
likes Minami Minamida.

379
19:35.362 --> 19:36.738
Romantically.

380
19:40.784 --> 19:42.286
What's that?

381
19:42.369 --> 19:43.578
You two watched the sunset.

382
19:44.997 --> 19:45.831
Yes.

383
19:49.084 --> 19:51.169
Ririi, do you know the answer?

384
19:52.170 --> 19:53.005
Well, yes.

385
19:53.880 --> 19:54.715
Tell me.

386
19:54.798 --> 19:56.091
That defeats the point.

387
19:56.174 --> 19:57.843
Tell me!

388
19:57.926 --> 19:59.094
Not telling!

389
19:59.177 --> 20:00.012
Tell me!

390
20:00.095 --> 20:01.555
Come on, let's play again. Clear up.

391
20:01.638 --> 20:02.723
Ririi, tell me.

392
20:08.645 --> 20:09.479
MINAMI MINAMIDA

393
20:09.563 --> 20:11.356
Before we visit Ray Arrows tomorrow,

394
20:11.440 --> 20:13.233
I have a question.

395
20:15.736 --> 20:16.903
A question?

396
20:17.446 --> 20:18.488
Of course.

397
20:19.865 --> 20:21.199
Is it about work?

398
20:23.660 --> 20:25.287
Or about whales?

399
20:30.375 --> 20:31.209
Your girlfriend?

400
20:31.293 --> 20:33.337
No, it's not.

401
20:33.420 --> 20:35.339
You look happy.

402
20:35.422 --> 20:36.631
Making plans for a date?

403
20:36.715 --> 20:38.008
It's about work.

404
20:38.717 --> 20:40.052
You crossed your arms.

405
20:41.011 --> 20:41.845
So?

406
20:43.430 --> 20:45.849
A detective I know told me

407
20:45.932 --> 20:47.726
when people lie,

408
20:47.809 --> 20:49.603
they don't want to get caught.

409
20:49.686 --> 20:52.189
Their urge to protect themselves grows.

410
20:52.898 --> 20:55.817
That state of mind makes them

411
20:55.901 --> 20:59.529
cross their arms to form a physical barrier.

412
21:02.908 --> 21:04.701
Or cross their legs.

413
21:07.371 --> 21:08.955
You're popular with women.

414
21:09.039 --> 21:11.333
Don't let the other women here find out.

415
21:12.501 --> 21:14.044
Who is it?

416
21:14.127 --> 21:15.796
Someone here? A lawyer?

417
21:16.254 --> 21:17.881
No, it's nothing like that.

418
21:17.964 --> 21:19.424
Just administrative work.

419
21:19.508 --> 21:21.968
Now you're covering your mouth.

420
21:22.052 --> 21:23.595
What? This too?

421
21:30.727 --> 21:33.939
I have a question before we visit Ray Arrows.

422
21:43.949 --> 21:45.242
Good morning.

423
21:45.867 --> 21:47.119
Good morning.

424
21:48.203 --> 21:49.830
Shall we go, then?

425
21:52.207 --> 21:53.417
Yes.

426
21:54.835 --> 21:58.004
A detective who's a friend of a friend said

427
21:58.088 --> 22:00.382
people cross their arms

428
22:00.465 --> 22:02.551
or legs when they're lying.

429
22:04.344 --> 22:06.638
Cross their arms and legs?

430
22:06.721 --> 22:09.516
Yes. I think it's fairly accurate.

431
22:09.599 --> 22:11.685
And putting a hand over your mouth

432
22:11.768 --> 22:14.146
apparently means you want to hide a lie.

433
22:16.314 --> 22:17.732
Ririi said eyes.

434
22:17.816 --> 22:20.152
Dad said to watch the nose.

435
22:20.235 --> 22:23.196
So I have to watch eyes, noses, mouths,

436
22:23.280 --> 22:26.199
and the whole body at once?

437
22:27.409 --> 22:29.035
That's very difficult.

438
22:39.462 --> 22:41.131
About what I just said,

439
22:41.965 --> 22:43.842
don't get too caught up in it.

440
22:43.925 --> 22:46.178
Maybe just talk as you normally would.

441
22:46.887 --> 22:48.388
Trust your instincts.

442
22:51.224 --> 22:52.934
My instincts are often wrong.

443
22:53.852 --> 22:55.437
Many autistic people

444
22:55.937 --> 22:58.398
are easily deceived and can't lie.

445
22:59.191 --> 23:00.317
I'm one of them.

446
23:01.610 --> 23:04.237
If being fooled were a competition,

447
23:04.321 --> 23:05.906
I'd make the podium.

448
23:07.908 --> 23:11.912
Because autistic people are more innocent?

449
23:14.623 --> 23:16.625
Not so much innocent…

450
23:19.586 --> 23:20.837
Most people

451
23:21.379 --> 23:24.174
live in a world with themselves and others.

452
23:25.133 --> 23:26.343
But autistic people

453
23:26.968 --> 23:29.262
live in a world of their own.

454
23:30.388 --> 23:31.973
I think that's why.

455
23:34.434 --> 23:36.645
A world of their own?

456
23:37.687 --> 23:38.647
Yes.

457
23:39.606 --> 23:42.776
I know people think differently from me

458
23:43.443 --> 23:45.612
and might deceive me.

459
23:45.695 --> 23:48.615
But even knowing that, I forget.

460
23:49.324 --> 23:52.369
In today's interviews, for instance,

461
23:52.452 --> 23:54.162
the Ray Arrows staff

462
23:54.246 --> 23:57.207
may lie to please the chairman.

463
23:57.791 --> 23:59.876
To avoid being deceived,

464
23:59.960 --> 24:02.921
I have to keep thinking, "Don't be fooled."

465
24:03.421 --> 24:05.090
I have to stay conscious of it.

466
24:07.092 --> 24:08.760
That's helpful to know.

467
24:11.096 --> 24:12.264
It helps?

468
24:12.847 --> 24:13.932
I mean…

469
24:14.015 --> 24:17.811
It's very helpful for understanding you.

470
24:20.230 --> 24:22.357
In that sense, it is helpful.

471
24:33.660 --> 24:35.620
Taking a break, Mr. Himi?

472
24:36.413 --> 24:39.666
Ms. Minamida and Mr. Funai went to see the client.

473
24:40.625 --> 24:42.585
There they go meddling again.

474
24:43.670 --> 24:46.006
More importantly, Ms. Asahi, are you okay

475
24:46.089 --> 24:48.174
with Funai and Minamida being together?

476
24:50.010 --> 24:50.844
What?

477
24:50.927 --> 24:53.346
You know, office romance.

478
24:54.097 --> 24:57.434
When people spend time together, it can happen.

479
24:58.101 --> 25:00.770
Then again, Ms. Minamida's no threat.

480
25:02.439 --> 25:04.691
You must have a lot of free time.

481
25:05.608 --> 25:08.278
I'm only saying this to support you.

482
25:10.864 --> 25:11.698
What?

483
25:11.781 --> 25:15.118
The person Funai likes…

484
25:15.201 --> 25:18.538
I think it might be you, Ms. Asahi.

485
25:18.621 --> 25:20.206
What?

486
25:20.290 --> 25:22.167
Did Mr. Funai say something?

487
25:23.043 --> 25:24.794
About me? To you?

488
25:24.878 --> 25:26.129
Curious?

489
25:29.799 --> 25:31.009
No, no…

490
25:31.926 --> 25:33.053
Not really.

491
25:39.601 --> 25:42.103
Shall we practice, then?

492
25:42.187 --> 25:45.690
Ask me questions as if I work at Ray Arrows.

493
25:46.900 --> 25:47.984
Understood.

494
25:51.988 --> 25:54.866
Look into my eyes, please.

495
26:00.580 --> 26:02.207
Ask me anything.

496
26:05.377 --> 26:06.503
Here goes.

497
26:09.255 --> 26:12.258
Minato Funai likes Minami Minamida.

498
26:12.342 --> 26:13.718
Is that true?

499
26:15.220 --> 26:16.304
What?

500
26:17.305 --> 26:19.682
Is it true or false?

501
26:31.152 --> 26:32.404
Well…

502
26:40.995 --> 26:42.831
For a member of staff,

503
26:43.998 --> 26:45.834
that's a difficult question.

504
26:51.881 --> 26:52.924
That's right.

505
26:53.675 --> 26:55.885
This is interview practice.

506
27:09.441 --> 27:12.068
Class sizes are like this everywhere.

507
27:12.944 --> 27:14.028
The mouth…

508
27:16.739 --> 27:19.868
Depends how particular you want to be.

509
27:20.535 --> 27:21.494
The arms?

510
27:24.622 --> 27:25.748
Right.

511
27:25.832 --> 27:28.209
Ms. Saty's on a different level from us.

512
27:29.043 --> 27:30.170
Nose and eyes?

513
27:36.968 --> 27:39.804
And how are you treated here?

514
27:39.888 --> 27:41.806
Well, it's not really about that…

515
27:45.268 --> 27:47.228
Please let me see your face.

516
27:47.312 --> 27:49.272
Hello, everyone.

517
27:49.355 --> 27:50.523
Hello.

518
27:50.607 --> 27:51.483
A treat.

519
27:51.566 --> 27:54.569
Sometimes we get those special tarts.

520
27:54.652 --> 27:55.695
It's a nice perk.

521
27:55.778 --> 27:57.864
Here we go! Ta-da!

522
27:59.365 --> 28:01.534
This one looks the best.

523
28:01.618 --> 28:02.827
It's huge!

524
28:02.911 --> 28:04.245
Wow. Which one?

525
28:04.329 --> 28:06.623
Can I have this one?

526
28:06.706 --> 28:08.541
Everyone, stop.

527
28:08.625 --> 28:10.960
You crossed your arms and legs.

528
28:11.044 --> 28:12.921
What are you all hiding?

529
28:19.219 --> 28:23.556
I hoped to find at least one more clue than Mr. Himi.

530
28:24.974 --> 28:27.352
But I have to wonder,

531
28:27.435 --> 28:30.313
is this really worth suing over?

532
28:30.396 --> 28:32.273
Saty has her approach.

533
28:32.357 --> 28:36.736
Ray Arrows has theirs. Isn't that all it is?

534
28:44.118 --> 28:44.953
Ms. Minamida?

535
28:46.704 --> 28:48.081
Those orange shoes.

536
28:49.165 --> 28:50.917
Yuma and his friends wore them too.

537
28:51.709 --> 28:53.336
These are specially designed, right?

538
28:53.419 --> 28:56.923
They had the same little smiley face on theirs.

539
28:59.425 --> 29:02.846
We all used to be students here.

540
29:03.429 --> 29:06.474
We were in Ms. Saty's class, aiming for the competition.

541
29:07.141 --> 29:10.144
We got matching shoes before entering.

542
29:11.521 --> 29:13.147
Only you stayed?

543
29:14.440 --> 29:17.235
I wanted to keep studying here.

544
29:19.070 --> 29:21.489
But you even got matching shoes.

545
29:21.990 --> 29:24.742
Didn't you want to compete alongside them?

546
29:25.743 --> 29:26.619
Not really…

547
29:27.120 --> 29:28.580
Competitions, I…

548
29:29.080 --> 29:30.456
I'm not interested.

549
29:35.211 --> 29:36.254
Her mouth…

550
29:36.337 --> 29:37.505
She touched it.

551
30:04.657 --> 30:06.868
What did you want to discuss?

552
30:06.951 --> 30:07.911
Yes.

553
30:07.994 --> 30:12.081
Regarding the civil suit against Fordee Dance Studio,

554
30:12.165 --> 30:13.625
I suggest withdrawing it.

555
30:14.083 --> 30:14.918
What?

556
30:15.001 --> 30:17.420
What? You want to give up?

557
30:17.503 --> 30:19.422
I'm not dropping the lawsuit.

558
30:19.505 --> 30:20.381
Yes.

559
30:20.465 --> 30:25.970
We'll drop the defamation claim for damages against Saty

560
30:26.054 --> 30:28.640
and sue Fordee Dance Studio instead

561
30:28.723 --> 30:30.892
in a new lawsuit.

562
30:30.975 --> 30:33.353
Why go to all that trouble?

563
30:34.062 --> 30:38.483
You just resent me taking the lead on this case, don't you?

564
30:38.566 --> 30:40.276
That's not true.

565
30:40.360 --> 30:44.113
I've found a more reliable way to secure damages.

566
30:44.197 --> 30:45.698
-Chairman. -Well…

567
30:47.158 --> 30:48.368
Let's hear her out.

568
30:51.913 --> 30:54.123
Minato, your help, please.

569
31:08.972 --> 31:12.892
We focused only on what Saty's posts said.

570
31:12.976 --> 31:15.395
We should've looked at the dates.

571
31:17.021 --> 31:20.650
Saty left Ray Arrows on June 30.

572
31:27.490 --> 31:28.658
RAY ARROWS JUNE - SATY RESIGNS

573
31:28.741 --> 31:32.036
Yes. Her contract ran through June.

574
31:32.120 --> 31:34.956
And Fordee Dance Studio

575
31:35.039 --> 31:37.417
opened on August 1st.

576
31:38.626 --> 31:40.253
FORDEE DANCE STUDIO OPEN - 14 TRANSFERS

577
31:40.336 --> 31:44.007
They're now training for next month's competition.

578
31:46.300 --> 31:48.261
RAY ARROWS SEP - 397, 21 LEFT OCT - 342, 34 LEFT

579
31:48.344 --> 31:52.724
The unit representing Fordee Dance Studio at the competition,

580
31:52.807 --> 31:54.350
Team Nikori,

581
31:54.434 --> 31:57.729
is made up entirely of former Ray Arrows students.

582
31:57.812 --> 32:00.273
A photo of them in matching shoes

583
32:00.356 --> 32:02.984
was posted on June 1st.

584
32:06.863 --> 32:08.072
JUNE, JULY, AUGUST…

585
32:08.156 --> 32:12.368
So when did Saty enter them in the competition?

586
32:13.578 --> 32:16.080
I contacted the organizers.

587
32:16.164 --> 32:18.666
They said that, as of June 10,

588
32:18.750 --> 32:21.961
Team Nikori was already entered under Fordee Dance Studio.

589
32:22.837 --> 32:24.088
June?

590
32:24.172 --> 32:25.715
She was still under contract to us.

591
32:26.799 --> 32:31.929
I reviewed the employment contract between Saty and Ray Arrows.

592
32:32.013 --> 32:35.224
It states that if she sets up a competing business,

593
32:35.308 --> 32:37.810
she may not poach their clients.

594
32:38.603 --> 32:41.606
In other words, Saty's actions constitute poaching

595
32:41.689 --> 32:43.066
and appear to breach her contract.

596
32:43.900 --> 32:45.777
Now I see!

597
32:45.860 --> 32:47.028
As a result,

598
32:47.111 --> 32:49.739
Ray Arrows not only lost students,

599
32:49.822 --> 32:53.076
but a valuable publicity opportunity at the competition,

600
32:53.159 --> 32:56.579
and potentially a chance to recruit new students.

601
32:57.163 --> 32:58.289
The resulting losses

602
32:58.372 --> 33:02.794
likely exceed the damages claimed for defamation.

603
33:02.877 --> 33:06.005
This could really hurt her.

604
33:07.381 --> 33:08.925
Ms. Minami Minamida,

605
33:09.008 --> 33:11.135
I'm going with your plan!

606
33:11.219 --> 33:13.679
Then keep the defamation claim

607
33:13.763 --> 33:15.556
and just add breach of contract…

608
33:15.640 --> 33:16.933
Then, Mr. Himi,

609
33:17.016 --> 33:21.312
did you obtain any testimony proving that her posts were false?

610
33:22.355 --> 33:23.439
Well…

611
33:24.023 --> 33:26.025
Then we'll withdraw

612
33:26.109 --> 33:29.695
the defamation damages claim against Saty

613
33:29.779 --> 33:31.989
and file a new claim

614
33:32.073 --> 33:34.951
for damages for breach of contract.

615
33:35.034 --> 33:36.702
Any objections?

616
33:47.171 --> 33:48.297
This way.

617
33:50.842 --> 33:51.801
Hello.

618
33:51.884 --> 33:52.802
Hello.

619
33:52.885 --> 33:54.595
She works under me.

620
33:54.679 --> 33:58.558
My client, Mr. Watagami, Medical Association president.

621
33:59.308 --> 34:00.351
I'm Minami Minamida.

622
34:01.060 --> 34:03.688
Forwards or backwards, Minami Minamida.

623
34:03.771 --> 34:06.774
Kayak, deed, rotator, civic, racecar, Minami Minamida.

624
34:07.650 --> 34:08.693
She's interesting.

625
34:09.402 --> 34:11.195
Is she handling the Ray Arrows case?

626
34:11.279 --> 34:12.321
Yes.

627
34:13.239 --> 34:16.367
Yes. I'm handling that case.

628
34:16.450 --> 34:19.704
I heard you're withdrawing one suit to file another.

629
34:19.787 --> 34:21.539
You've heard already?

630
34:21.622 --> 34:23.541
So will the traffic congestion

631
34:23.624 --> 34:26.210
clear up sooner than planned?

632
34:28.629 --> 34:30.089
Traffic congestion?

633
34:30.173 --> 34:31.674
Sooner than planned?

634
34:31.757 --> 34:33.134
Sir, we should go.

635
34:34.468 --> 34:35.803
I'm counting on you.

636
34:37.305 --> 34:38.514
-See you. -Goodbye.

637
34:44.103 --> 34:45.563
That's why they're suing?

638
34:47.398 --> 34:48.524
Ms. Minamida?

639
34:55.781 --> 34:59.118
BREACH OF CONTRACT FIRST ORAL ARGUMENT

640
34:59.785 --> 35:02.914
Plaintiff's counsel, you may examine the witness.

641
35:06.834 --> 35:08.377
Ms. Minamida?

642
35:08.461 --> 35:10.004
Plaintiff's counsel?

643
35:13.758 --> 35:14.592
Yes.

644
35:14.675 --> 35:16.052
Never mind. I'll do it.

645
35:16.636 --> 35:18.888
I'm Himi, counsel for the plaintiff.

646
35:20.514 --> 35:21.933
The defendant asked you

647
35:22.016 --> 35:24.977
to transfer to Fordee Dance Studio, correct?

648
35:25.061 --> 35:26.938
When was that?

649
35:27.688 --> 35:28.898
May…

650
35:29.565 --> 35:31.692
11th, I think.

651
35:31.776 --> 35:35.488
She asked six of us in the select class to stay behind.

652
35:36.155 --> 35:37.240
That's when…

653
35:37.740 --> 35:41.369
So she invited you to transfer

654
35:41.452 --> 35:43.621
while she was still employed at Ray Arrows?

655
35:46.123 --> 35:46.958
Yes.

656
35:48.668 --> 35:51.629
But you've stayed at Ray Arrows.

657
35:52.255 --> 35:53.256
Why is that?

658
35:55.299 --> 35:56.634
Actually…

659
35:56.717 --> 35:58.636
I wanted to compete too…

660
36:01.931 --> 36:03.391
But Ms. Saty said

661
36:04.058 --> 36:08.229
it would be hard for me to do that and attend cram school.

662
36:08.312 --> 36:09.397
I see.

663
36:10.273 --> 36:13.859
Poaching talented students and winning competitions

664
36:13.943 --> 36:15.486
would be great publicity.

665
36:16.070 --> 36:18.781
-The defendant's intent… -What's wrong with that?

666
36:24.287 --> 36:25.579
I just…

667
36:27.248 --> 36:29.959
I didn't want their talent to go to waste!

668
36:30.042 --> 36:33.254
I can help those children develop their talents!

669
36:40.469 --> 36:41.804
Making excuses?

670
36:41.887 --> 36:43.597
Poaching is a breach of contract.

671
36:43.681 --> 36:46.225
Your Honor, she shows no remorse.

672
36:47.226 --> 36:49.854
The defendant will refrain from interrupting.

673
36:50.771 --> 36:51.981
I'm sorry.

674
36:57.987 --> 37:02.366
Regardless of motive, the poaching appears to breach the contract.

675
37:02.450 --> 37:04.285
That's my view at present.

676
37:07.663 --> 37:09.457
Thank you for everything.

677
37:14.503 --> 37:15.421
Yuma.

678
37:16.130 --> 37:17.256
Don't stop dancing.

679
37:51.415 --> 37:52.375
Hello.

680
37:52.875 --> 37:54.001
Hello.

681
37:55.586 --> 37:58.839
Fordee Dance Studio withdrew from the competition, I hear.

682
37:58.923 --> 38:00.633
They just posted a notice.

683
38:01.717 --> 38:04.428
It seems they wanted to protect the kids from backlash.

684
38:05.638 --> 38:08.849
Paying damages will hurt their business too.

685
38:11.352 --> 38:12.520
Right.

686
38:12.603 --> 38:15.147
This tart's from the Medical Association head.

687
38:15.648 --> 38:16.816
The Medical Association head?

688
38:16.899 --> 38:19.985
Yes. I'm not sure, but Mr. Himi said

689
38:20.069 --> 38:22.196
it might be thanks for the Ray Arrows suit.

690
38:32.581 --> 38:34.291
Excuse me a moment.

691
38:39.088 --> 38:41.090
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

692
38:58.524 --> 39:00.776
FORDEE DANCE STUDIO

693
39:12.246 --> 39:13.789
Hello.

694
39:16.542 --> 39:17.626
Mr. Himi.

695
39:18.627 --> 39:21.630
How is Ray Arrows linked to the Medical Association head?

696
39:21.714 --> 39:23.716
What?

697
39:23.799 --> 39:26.635
Apparently, his eldest child went to school

698
39:26.719 --> 39:28.429
with a Ray Arrows board member.

699
39:28.512 --> 39:29.680
Is that all?

700
39:30.306 --> 39:33.267
Watagami Hospital, being demolished near Fordee…

701
39:34.101 --> 39:36.437
Isn't it connected to this lawsuit?

702
39:36.520 --> 39:37.438
I don't know.

703
39:37.521 --> 39:38.939
Please don't play dumb.

704
39:43.777 --> 39:45.237
Well…

705
39:45.321 --> 39:47.364
This is just speculation,

706
39:48.574 --> 39:50.743
but land that size in that location

707
39:50.826 --> 39:52.870
could sell for billions of yen.

708
39:52.953 --> 39:54.663
Maybe tens of billions.

709
39:55.664 --> 39:59.460
However, its property value also depends on the surrounding area.

710
39:59.543 --> 40:02.922
If it puts an end to the neighborhood's chronic traffic congestion,

711
40:03.005 --> 40:05.132
it'd be worth the legal costs to the president.

712
40:05.716 --> 40:08.511
So Ray Arrows was a front

713
40:08.594 --> 40:09.762
for a SLAPP suit.

714
40:09.845 --> 40:12.348
That's one way to look at it.

715
40:14.141 --> 40:16.602
Besides, I think Ms. Minamida

716
40:16.685 --> 40:18.729
had figured that much out too.

717
40:18.812 --> 40:19.897
What?

718
40:20.564 --> 40:22.983
That's why she acted strangely

719
40:23.067 --> 40:24.193
at the witness examination.

720
40:25.986 --> 40:30.866
She and I both worked to maximize our client's interests.

721
40:31.575 --> 40:32.826
Isn't that enough?

722
40:51.720 --> 40:52.763
Ms. Minamida.

723
40:55.307 --> 40:56.684
What's wrong?

724
41:01.689 --> 41:02.773
I see.

725
41:02.856 --> 41:04.942
It's about Fordee Dance Studio.

726
41:05.651 --> 41:06.610
Yes.

727
41:08.946 --> 41:09.989
I…

728
41:11.240 --> 41:13.826
I think I did something unnecessary.

729
41:13.909 --> 41:15.119
Unnecessary?

730
41:16.787 --> 41:18.414
The breach of contract suit.

731
41:19.957 --> 41:23.752
If we'd let the defamation case drag on,

732
41:24.670 --> 41:27.965
the children might have been able to compete.

733
41:30.593 --> 41:32.678
But Ms. Saty said

734
41:33.721 --> 41:36.765
breach her contract. That's a fact.

735
41:37.308 --> 41:41.437
So, as a lawyer, you did the right thing, didn't you?

736
41:44.315 --> 41:46.859
Even if it was right as a lawyer,

737
41:47.776 --> 41:51.447
it didn't feel right as Minami Minamida.

738
41:51.947 --> 41:54.491
But Minami Minamida is a lawyer.

739
41:57.786 --> 41:59.538
The more I think about it,

740
42:00.205 --> 42:01.999
the less I understand.

741
42:06.337 --> 42:10.924
Did you know the real purpose of that lawsuit, Mr. Miyaji?

742
42:11.008 --> 42:13.052
No. I didn't.

743
42:19.433 --> 42:21.435
Well, I can't quite say that.

744
42:23.145 --> 42:24.396
If I knew,

745
42:24.480 --> 42:27.608
I'd have to take a stand one way or another.

746
42:28.150 --> 42:29.568
So I avoided knowing.

747
42:31.320 --> 42:32.488
That's pretty unfair of me.

748
42:33.322 --> 42:34.740
Yes. It is unfair.

749
42:38.577 --> 42:40.829
At some point, I started

750
42:40.913 --> 42:44.958
accepting that this is just what being a lawyer means.

751
42:47.252 --> 42:50.214
Will I become like that someday?

752
42:50.297 --> 42:51.632
That

753
42:52.257 --> 42:56.804
depends on what kind of lawyer you want to be, doesn't it?

754
42:59.431 --> 43:01.392
What kind of lawyer I want to be?

755
43:04.687 --> 43:05.854
I should get going.

756
43:16.115 --> 43:18.742
What kind of lawyer…

757
43:18.826 --> 43:20.369
Do I want to be?

758
43:22.329 --> 43:25.416
I'd hoped you would take my case, Ms. Yamaoka.

759
43:25.499 --> 43:26.875
I'm sorry.

760
43:26.959 --> 43:29.169
I'd like to take it,

761
43:29.253 --> 43:32.756
but I'm winding up my current cases one by one.

762
43:32.840 --> 43:37.302
Are you following your father into politics, then?

763
43:37.386 --> 43:38.762
That's the rumor.

764
43:41.890 --> 43:44.184
You have my full support.

765
43:48.814 --> 43:50.107
Come in.

766
43:50.190 --> 43:51.942
Your car is ready.

767
43:52.860 --> 43:54.111
I'll be going, then.

768
43:54.194 --> 43:55.738
Thank you very much.

769
43:59.700 --> 44:01.869
The documents you requested.

770
44:01.952 --> 44:02.870
Thank you.

771
44:10.502 --> 44:12.004
ATTEMPTED MURDER CASE JUDGMENT

772
44:12.087 --> 44:13.756
DEFENSE COUNSEL - MIYAJI, MINAMIDA

773
44:16.675 --> 44:18.677
DEFENSE COUNSEL - MIYAJI, HIMI, MINAMIDA

774
44:22.014 --> 44:23.932
RAY ARROWS DANCE ACADEMY YASUO MITSUYA

775
44:28.020 --> 44:31.023
MINAMI MINAMIDA LAWYER HIROKAWA &amp; HOWARD LPC

776
44:31.106 --> 44:32.065
MINAMI MINAMIDA

777
44:35.152 --> 44:37.237
AN AUTISTIC LAWYER IS BORN!

778
44:44.703 --> 44:49.708
Subtitle translation by: Hasan Hüseyin Öztürk

779
44:50.292 --> 44:52.002
Those two would make a good couple.

780
44:52.085 --> 44:55.589
Like my heart's being squeezed into a salted rice ball.

781
44:55.672 --> 44:56.798
That's jealousy.

782
44:56.882 --> 44:59.009
Opposing counsel is Yasuko Yamaoka.

783
44:59.092 --> 45:01.553
Did you hire Minami because you could use her?

784
45:01.637 --> 45:04.014
Let's thoroughly research this railway project.

785
45:04.097 --> 45:07.017
Not sure you like him? Try touching him.

786
45:07.768 --> 45:10.896
Dad, you're always interfering in my life.

787
45:11.522 --> 45:13.732
I can't even fail on my own!
